        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4486a4da-d99e-5475-a258-3c9a33e62269",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Emilio Botín, José María Amusategui\n- Companies: Banco Santander, Banco Español de Crédito (Banesto), Banco Central Hispano, Banco Santander Central Hispano (BSCH), Santander Group\n- Topics: bank acquisitions and mergers, Spanish banking\n\nFacts:\n- In 1993, Emilio Botín's bank absorbed Banco Español de Crédito (Banesto).\n- In 1999, Banco Santander merged with Banco Central Hispano to create Banco Santander Central Hispano (BSCH).\n- In 1999, Banco Santander Central Hispano became Spain's largest bank.\n- From 1999 until 2002, Emilio Botín and José María Amusategui served as co-presidents of Banco Santander Central Hispano.\n- In 2002, José María Amusategui retired from Banco Santander Central Hispano.\n- The Santander Group is a Spanish banking group centered on Banco Santander, S.A.",
